> # --- scene MASK (scene_mask.py, front_clearance_node) -------------------------
> # The whole-frame, ROI-free per-pixel classification the rebuilt wall pipeline
> # consumes: SELF > OBJECT > FLOOR > REFLECTION > CEILING > WALL > INVALID, in
> # that priority. It exists because the ROI front distance reads whatever fills
> # a fixed rectangle, and on an open corridor that is the FLOOR
> # (/perception/front_distance sat at ~2.0 m with nothing ahead for 10 m,
> # corridor_phantom 2026-10-15). Publishes /perception/scene_labels/image (only
> # when subscribed), /perception/wall_points and /perception/scene_labels/stats.
> front_clearance_scene_mask_enabled:
>   default: true
>   description: "Run the whole-frame scene mask (scene_mask.py) in front_clearance_node. Independent of enable_scene_labels, which still drives the older ROI stereo wall distance; the two coexist until the ROI path is retired."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_rate_hz:
>   default: 5.0
>   description: "Rate [Hz] of the scene-mask tick. Measured 10.5 ms per 640x360 frame for classify + WALL points + stats (test_scene_mask.py), so 5 Hz is ~5% of one core; the depth stream itself runs at 30 Hz. 0 disables the tick."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_floor_tol_m:
>   default: 0.05
>   description: "Half-height [m] of the band around z = 0 that is FLOOR; below -this is REFLECTION. base_link's z = 0 IS the floor (base.xacro), so this is pure measurement error: the ZED mount pitch is measured to 2.083 deg (camera.launch.py) and the height to 0.205 m, which at 3 m is about 1 cm of height error. 5 cm covers that plus floor unevenness without reaching a kerb. UNTUNED against a bag with depth."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_ceiling_min_z_m:
>   default: 2.0
>   description: "Height [m] above which a point is CEILING. Matches front_clearance_scene_ceiling_min_m, the lower edge of the band the older CeilingTracker searches for the ceiling peak, so the two agree on what can possibly be ceiling. Well above the 1.0 m front_clearance_scene_max_relevant_height_m, so a door lintel or a shelf stays WALL rather than being written off as ceiling."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_min_depth_m:
>   default: 0.2
>   description: "Depth [m] below which a pixel has no usable measurement. The ZED's minimum measurable range on this rig; nearer than this the driver publishes -Inf, which is a real 'something is right there' reading and is counted in the stats as too_close_frac rather than being merged into 'no data'."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_max_depth_m:
>   default: 20.0
>   description: "Depth [m] above which a pixel is not a usable measurement. Matches the LiDAR's own measured ~20 m ceiling (99.9th pct 19.89 m), so stereo and LiDAR agree about where 'no reading' starts. Stereo noise grows with the square of range and is metres by 20 m; the floor far rows run past this and correctly become INVALID rather than a false FLOOR."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_strip_half_width_m:
>   default: 0.186
>   description: "Half-width [m] of the car-width strip the scene-mask stats count WALL points in. MUST equal vehicle_frames.front_side_limit_m() (swept_clearance_body_half_width_m 0.136 + front_beside_body_margin_m 0.05): one strip for the whole pipeline, so 'the camera sees a wall in the way' and 'the LiDAR sees a wall in the way' mean the same geometry. Overridable only to test; the node's default IS the shared helper."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_self_polygons:
>   default: ""
>   description: "SELF-mask polygons as JSON [[[x, y], ...], ...] in FRACTIONS of image width/height (a ROS parameter cannot hold a ragged nested list). EMPTY, the default, derives the one polygon from lidar_exclusion_x_min/_x_max/_y_min/_y_max, the car's-own-LiDAR-housing rectangle yolo_detector_node already applies to detections: one calibration, now three consumers, and no second copy of the numbers to drift. Set this only to override that rectangle with a real polygon once one has been traced on a frame."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_occluded_polygons:
>   default: '[[[0.0, 0.78], [0.16, 0.78], [0.16, 1.0], [0.0, 1.0]]]'
>   description: "Further SELF-mask polygons, same JSON format, for the region where the housing occludes the RIGHT lens: the left image has scene there but no correct stereo match, so the depth is the housing's. Separate from front_clearance_scene_mask_self_polygons so the depth-only region can be tuned without touching the shared housing rectangle. UNTUNED placeholder: no bag with depth has been inspected for its real extent."
> front_clearance_scene_mask_image_topic:
>   default: "/camera/image_raw"
>   description: "Left RGB image the scene-mask overlay is drawn on. Decoded ONLY when /perception/scene_labels/image has a subscriber, the same draw-when-watched discipline the annotated detection image follows."
